  "abstract": "Red Hat Storage Server is a software only, scale-out storage solution that\nprovides flexible and agile unstructured data storage for the enterprise.\n\nThe updated Red Hat Storage Server packages include numerous bug fixes and\nenhancements in Geo-replication. With this update, Quota is a fully supported\nfeature. It also introduces support for In-Service Rolling Upgrade, which\nenables you to upgrade to the latest version without stopping the replicated and\ndistributed-replicated volumes. Space precludes documenting all of these changes\nin this advisory. Users are directed to the Red Hat Storage 2.1 Technical Notes\nfor information on the most significant of these changes:\n\nhttps://access.redhat.com/site/documentation/en-US/Red_Hat_Storage/2.1/html/Technical_Notes/index.html\n\nUsers of Red Hat Storage are advised to upgrade to these updated packages, which\nfix these bugs and add these enhancements.\n",
